Construct the known component $\mathbf{a}$ from $O$, ending at $A$. Count signed horizontal and vertical grid displacements:

$$
\begin{aligned}
\overrightarrow{OA} &=1\,(0, 3)=(0, 3). \\
\overrightarrow{AC} &=(-6, 0).
\end{aligned}
$$

![](images/25/253a9bb53856676892d4b19429783d7741578efa0a30aab163fe9b410275cf49.png)

Compare the remaining displacement with $\mathbf{b}$, whose grid displacement is $(-4, 0)$:

$$
\begin{aligned}
\text{Horizontal scale} &=\frac{-6}{-4}=\frac{3}{2}
\end{aligned}
$$

The scale is positive, so the remaining vector has the same direction as $\mathbf{b}$. Thus $\overrightarrow{AC}=\frac{3}{2}\mathbf{b}$. By the triangle law,

$$
\begin{aligned}
\mathbf{c} &=\overrightarrow{OA}+\overrightarrow{AC} \\
&=\mathbf{a}+\frac{3}{2}\mathbf{b} \\
&=\mathbf{a}+\frac{3}{2}\mathbf{b}.
\end{aligned}
$$

The vectors $\mathbf{a}$ and $\mathbf{b}$ are not parallel, so their coefficients are unique. Matching the coefficient of $\mathbf{b}$ gives $\lambda=\frac{3}{2}$.

Construct the known component $3\mathbf{a}$ from $O$, and call its endpoint $P$. Count signed horizontal and vertical grid displacements:

$$
\begin{aligned}
\overrightarrow{OP} &=3\,(1, -2)=(3, -6). \\
\overrightarrow{PC} &=(10, 0).
\end{aligned}
$$

![](images/7c/7c56b9da9e7851041289dc3d66c7482da6242031c5821f49a5a980774b5cc828.png)

Compare the remaining displacement with $\mathbf{b}$, whose grid displacement is $(4, 0)$:

$$
\begin{aligned}
\text{Horizontal scale} &=\frac{10}{4}=\frac{5}{2}
\end{aligned}
$$

The scale is positive, so the remaining vector has the same direction as $\mathbf{b}$. Thus $\overrightarrow{PC}=\frac{5}{2}\mathbf{b}$. By the triangle law,

$$
\begin{aligned}
\mathbf{c} &=\overrightarrow{OP}+\overrightarrow{PC} \\
&=3\mathbf{a}+\frac{5}{2}\mathbf{b} \\
&=3\mathbf{a}+\frac{5}{2}\mathbf{b}.
\end{aligned}
$$

The vectors $\mathbf{a}$ and $\mathbf{b}$ are not parallel, so their coefficients are unique. Matching the coefficient of $\mathbf{b}$ gives $\lambda=\frac{5}{2}$.
